@nazariig, @vaibhavhd - We hit this same crash (NULL deref in `lacp_event_watch_port_removing()` via the `port_obj_create()` rollback) on a 202511-based image, but with a different trigger than warm-reboot. 

During a cold `config reload`, a port listed in both `PORTCHANNEL_MEMBER` and `VLAN_MEMBER` was enslaved to the PortChannel by teammgrd and then moved into `Bridge` by vlanmgrd less than 1 ms later. teamd's `port_added` handling failed, and the rollback crashed in LACP. 

`0013-set-port-to-disabled-state-during-removal.patch` is identical on 202511, so that branch is exposed as well. Could this fix also be backported to 202511?

